AWS API Gateway Explained (A Core Service for Modern Applications)

Modern applications need a secure and scalable way to expose APIs to users and services.

That’s where Amazon API Gateway comes in.

Amazon API Gateway is a fully managed service that allows developers to create, publish, secure, and manage APIs at any scale.

It acts as the entry point for backend services running on AWS.

Key capabilities engineers should know:

🔹 Create REST and HTTP APIs easily
🔹 Secure APIs using IAM, API keys, or authentication tokens
🔹 Automatically scale to handle large numbers of requests
🔹 Monitor API traffic and performance using CloudWatch
🔹 Integrate with backend services like AWS Lambda, EC2, or DynamoDB

Common use cases include:

• Building serverless APIs
• Connecting mobile or web apps to backend services
• Creating microservice architectures
• Managing public or internal APIs

The main advantage is that developers can focus on building application logic while API Gateway handles traffic management, security, and scaling.

Understanding API Gateway is essential for anyone working with cloud-native or serverless architectures.
